1
00:00:00,710 --> 00:00:02,090
The people building artificial

2
00:00:02,130 --> 00:00:04,430
intelligence are building bunkers.

3
00:00:04,740 --> 00:00:06,050
Think about who they are.

4
00:00:06,290 --> 00:00:08,260
They see this technology up close,

5
00:00:08,300 --> 00:00:09,610
before the rest of us.

6
00:00:09,790 --> 00:00:10,910
The same technology that's

7
00:00:10,950 --> 00:00:12,650
about to reshape your job,

8
00:00:12,690 --> 00:00:13,580
your daily life,

9
00:00:13,620 --> 00:00:14,390
and the world your

10
00:00:14,430 --> 00:00:15,820
children grow up in.

11
00:00:16,140 --> 00:00:17,080
And some of them have

12
00:00:17,120 --> 00:00:18,550
built a place to hide.

13
00:00:18,750 --> 00:00:19,720
Underground.

14
00:00:19,760 --> 00:00:20,370
Behind a door

15
00:00:20,410 --> 00:00:21,890
filled with concrete.

16
00:00:22,050 --> 00:00:24,150
A door that only opens for a few.

17
00:00:24,490 --> 00:00:26,130
So what are they hiding from?

18
00:00:26,710 --> 00:00:28,490
One of them said it out loud.

19
00:00:28,840 --> 00:00:30,450
OpenAI's chief scientist

20
00:00:30,490 --> 00:00:31,070
at the time

21
00:00:31,110 --> 00:00:33,180
told a room of new researchers:

22
00:00:33,510 --> 00:00:34,920
"We're definitely going to build

23
00:00:34,960 --> 00:00:37,600
a bunker before we release AGI."

24
00:00:37,750 --> 00:00:38,890
AGI.

25
00:00:39,120 --> 00:00:41,260
A machine as smart as us.

26
00:00:41,560 --> 00:00:43,670
So the answer seems obvious.

27
00:00:43,710 --> 00:00:45,510
They're afraid of the machine.

28
00:00:45,880 --> 00:00:47,760
But no door stops a machine

29
00:00:47,800 --> 00:00:49,180
that's smarter than you.

30
00:00:49,430 --> 00:00:50,430
And they know it.

31
00:00:50,650 --> 00:00:51,650
They're building bunkers

32
00:00:51,690 --> 00:00:52,720
for a reason.

33
00:00:53,050 --> 00:00:54,180
But the reason might

34
00:00:54,220 --> 00:00:55,730
not be the machine.

35
00:00:56,360 --> 00:00:58,790
There are three obvious suspects.

36
00:00:59,000 --> 00:00:59,970
The bomb.

37
00:01:00,010 --> 00:01:01,010
The machine.

38
00:01:01,270 --> 00:01:02,960
And the chaos along the way.

39
00:01:03,300 --> 00:01:04,520
The fourth is written into

40
00:01:04,560 --> 00:01:06,530
the floor plans of new bunkers.

41
00:01:06,790 --> 00:01:08,020
The bomb first.

42
00:01:08,240 --> 00:01:09,170
That door filled

43
00:01:09,210 --> 00:01:10,790
with concrete is real.

44
00:01:10,850 --> 00:01:11,870
It's in Hawaii.

45
00:01:12,140 --> 00:01:13,790
Under Mark Zuckerberg's ranch,

46
00:01:13,830 --> 00:01:15,130
there's an underground shelter

47
00:01:15,170 --> 00:01:16,880
bigger than most houses.

48
00:01:17,080 --> 00:01:18,680
He says it's for storms.

49
00:01:18,770 --> 00:01:20,860
In his words: "a little shelter.

50
00:01:20,900 --> 00:01:22,060
It's like a basement."

51
00:01:22,390 --> 00:01:23,390
Fair enough.

52
00:01:23,540 --> 00:01:24,550
The owners don't love

53
00:01:24,590 --> 00:01:26,030
the word bunker.

54
00:01:26,590 --> 00:01:28,930
Last year, the comedian Theo Von

55
00:01:28,970 --> 00:01:30,490
asked the head of OpenAI

56
00:01:30,530 --> 00:01:31,870
whether he has one.

57
00:01:32,260 --> 00:01:33,420
Here's Sam Altman:

58
00:01:42,030 --> 00:01:43,030
Bombs.

59
00:01:43,160 --> 00:01:44,560
Not AI.

60
00:01:44,950 --> 00:01:46,430
The people who sell bunkers

61
00:01:46,470 --> 00:01:48,190
name old reasons, too.

62
00:01:48,440 --> 00:01:49,180
War.

63
00:01:49,220 --> 00:01:50,220
Pandemics.

64
00:01:50,440 --> 00:01:52,290
So the bomb is real.

65
00:01:52,510 --> 00:01:53,700
But it's the oldest reason

66
00:01:53,740 --> 00:01:54,740
in the book.

67
00:01:55,690 --> 00:01:57,710
And something here is new.

68
00:01:58,040 --> 00:01:59,920
This year, bunker makers began

69
00:01:59,960 --> 00:02:01,750
adding a reason to their list.

70
00:02:02,140 --> 00:02:03,940
Artificial intelligence.

71
00:02:04,360 --> 00:02:05,200
Is it the machine

72
00:02:05,240 --> 00:02:06,430
they're afraid of?

73
00:02:07,630 --> 00:02:09,190
It would make sense.

74
00:02:09,410 --> 00:02:11,030
A panel of more than 100

75
00:02:11,070 --> 00:02:13,230
experts says AI is already

76
00:02:13,270 --> 00:02:15,630
being used in real cyberattacks.

77
00:02:15,930 --> 00:02:17,100
That's today's AI.

78
00:02:17,140 --> 00:02:18,850
Now picture the one these

79
00:02:18,890 --> 00:02:20,840
companies are racing to build.

80
00:02:20,960 --> 00:02:22,610
Smarter than any of us,

81
00:02:22,650 --> 00:02:23,690
at everything.

82
00:02:24,080 --> 00:02:26,280
Say that machine turns against us.

83
00:02:26,470 --> 00:02:27,440
A bunker is built

84
00:02:27,480 --> 00:02:28,850
for things that pass.

85
00:02:28,890 --> 00:02:29,750
A storm.

86
00:02:29,790 --> 00:02:30,440
Fallout.

87
00:02:30,480 --> 00:02:31,510
A war.

88
00:02:31,790 --> 00:02:33,800
That machine doesn't pass.

89
00:02:33,950 --> 00:02:36,110
One day the door has to open.

90
00:02:36,210 --> 00:02:37,440
And it's still out there.

91
00:02:37,810 --> 00:02:39,690
And if the machine turns out well,

92
00:02:39,790 --> 00:02:41,680
nobody needs a bunker at all.

93
00:02:42,230 --> 00:02:43,240
The head of OpenAI

94
00:02:43,280 --> 00:02:44,570
has said it himself:

95
00:02:44,990 --> 00:02:45,980
"None of this is gonna

96
00:02:46,020 --> 00:02:48,330
help if AGI goes wrong."

97
00:02:48,630 --> 00:02:49,510
And that bunker

98
00:02:49,550 --> 00:02:50,550
from the beginning?

99
00:02:50,800 --> 00:02:52,030
The scientist who announced

100
00:02:52,070 --> 00:02:53,570
it added one detail:

101
00:02:53,990 --> 00:02:55,360
"Of course, it's going to be

102
00:02:55,400 --> 00:02:56,570
optional whether you want

103
00:02:56,610 --> 00:02:58,000
to get into the bunker."

104
00:02:59,000 --> 00:02:59,940
Optional.

105
00:02:59,980 --> 00:03:01,400
Some scientists doubt

106
00:03:01,440 --> 00:03:03,410
that machine is anywhere close.

107
00:03:03,650 --> 00:03:06,190
Near or far, the logic holds.

108
00:03:06,350 --> 00:03:07,710
The only protection against

109
00:03:07,750 --> 00:03:09,950
that machine is to build it right.

110
00:03:10,150 --> 00:03:11,050
Out here.

111
00:03:11,090 --> 00:03:12,280
Not down there.

112
00:03:12,490 --> 00:03:14,080
Cross the machine off the list.

113
00:03:15,370 --> 00:03:16,230
But then why are

114
00:03:16,270 --> 00:03:17,580
they still building?

115
00:03:18,740 --> 00:03:20,000
Tristan Harris used to

116
00:03:20,040 --> 00:03:21,210
work at Google.

117
00:03:21,370 --> 00:03:22,280
Today he's one of

118
00:03:22,320 --> 00:03:24,500
the industry's sharpest critics.

119
00:03:24,720 --> 00:03:26,160
This spring he said:

120
00:03:32,780 --> 00:03:33,820
Right now.

121
00:03:34,010 --> 00:03:35,520
He names no names.

122
00:03:35,570 --> 00:03:36,840
But if he's right,

123
00:03:36,880 --> 00:03:37,720
a bunker must be

124
00:03:37,760 --> 00:03:38,940
good for something.

125
00:03:39,180 --> 00:03:40,740
Ask the people who sell them.

126
00:03:40,890 --> 00:03:42,090
Most shelters are stocked

127
00:03:42,130 --> 00:03:43,820
for weeks or months.

128
00:03:43,980 --> 00:03:44,680
The biggest ones

129
00:03:44,720 --> 00:03:46,220
promise a few years.

130
00:03:46,350 --> 00:03:48,520
Sales promises, all of them.

131
00:03:48,780 --> 00:03:50,830
But every bunker is a clock.

132
00:03:50,950 --> 00:03:51,640
So what are they

133
00:03:51,680 --> 00:03:53,230
expecting to wait out?

134
00:03:53,580 --> 00:03:55,250
Inside the AI industry,

135
00:03:55,290 --> 00:03:58,050
many expect a major AI incident.

136
00:03:58,260 --> 00:03:59,660
Not killer robots.

137
00:03:59,860 --> 00:04:01,330
More like a cyberattack

138
00:04:01,370 --> 00:04:02,660
that takes down banks,

139
00:04:02,700 --> 00:04:04,670
the internet, maybe the power.

140
00:04:05,190 --> 00:04:06,230
And you've already seen

141
00:04:06,270 --> 00:04:07,860
how fragile that is.

142
00:04:08,050 --> 00:04:09,970
In November, one faulty router

143
00:04:10,010 --> 00:04:12,350
stopped takeoffs across America.

144
00:04:12,620 --> 00:04:13,750
For hours.

145
00:04:13,990 --> 00:04:15,440
No AI involved.

146
00:04:15,720 --> 00:04:17,400
Then the planes flew again.

147
00:04:17,680 --> 00:04:19,760
The chaos stays on the list.

148
00:04:19,900 --> 00:04:21,900
A bunker can carry you through it.

149
00:04:22,050 --> 00:04:23,050
For a while.

150
00:04:23,290 --> 00:04:24,720
But it can't run itself.

151
00:04:25,030 --> 00:04:26,180
It needs fuel.

152
00:04:26,220 --> 00:04:27,120
Filters.

153
00:04:27,160 --> 00:04:28,160
And people.

154
00:04:28,450 --> 00:04:29,020
And when the world

155
00:04:29,060 --> 00:04:30,680
outside stops working,

156
00:04:30,830 --> 00:04:32,510
who do those people answer to?

157
00:04:33,690 --> 00:04:34,840
Some years ago,

158
00:04:34,880 --> 00:04:36,820
the writer Douglas Rushkoff

159
00:04:36,860 --> 00:04:38,520
was brought to a luxury resort

160
00:04:38,560 --> 00:04:40,420
to give a talk about the future.

161
00:04:40,670 --> 00:04:41,970
Instead of an audience,

162
00:04:42,010 --> 00:04:43,220
five very rich

163
00:04:43,260 --> 00:04:44,620
investors walked in.

164
00:04:44,880 --> 00:04:45,760
Here's what they really

165
00:04:45,800 --> 00:04:47,750
wanted to know, as he tells it:

166
00:04:59,020 --> 00:05:00,980
Once money is worthless.

167
00:05:01,340 --> 00:05:03,680
They called that day "the Event."

168
00:05:03,940 --> 00:05:05,920
The day everything breaks down.

169
00:05:06,280 --> 00:05:07,260
They knew they'd need

170
00:05:07,300 --> 00:05:08,760
armed guards against what they

171
00:05:08,800 --> 00:05:10,890
called "the angry mobs."

172
00:05:11,090 --> 00:05:12,350
But after the Event,

173
00:05:12,390 --> 00:05:14,220
why would the guards still obey?

174
00:05:14,620 --> 00:05:15,820
They had ideas.

175
00:05:15,890 --> 00:05:18,000
Special locks on the food supply.

176
00:05:18,200 --> 00:05:19,700
Disciplinary collars.

177
00:05:19,800 --> 00:05:21,330
Robots as guards.

178
00:05:22,310 --> 00:05:23,290
Rushkoff offered

179
00:05:23,330 --> 00:05:24,590
a different answer.

180
00:05:24,830 --> 00:05:26,170
They rolled their eyes.

181
00:05:26,420 --> 00:05:27,650
That's his account.

182
00:05:27,800 --> 00:05:29,350
The men were never named.

183
00:05:29,470 --> 00:05:30,730
And they were investors,

184
00:05:30,770 --> 00:05:32,570
not the people who build AI.

185
00:05:32,790 --> 00:05:33,410
But look at what

186
00:05:33,450 --> 00:05:34,720
gets planned today.

187
00:05:35,290 --> 00:05:37,010
Some new bunker projects come

188
00:05:37,050 --> 00:05:39,240
with "anti-mutiny" procedures,

189
00:05:39,280 --> 00:05:40,160
so that guards,

190
00:05:40,200 --> 00:05:41,750
or anyone else inside,

191
00:05:41,790 --> 00:05:43,010
can't take over.

192
00:05:43,420 --> 00:05:44,340
Others are designed

193
00:05:44,380 --> 00:05:46,150
with "detention areas."

194
00:05:46,530 --> 00:05:47,820
The question from that room

195
00:05:47,860 --> 00:05:49,540
is now in the floor plans.

196
00:05:49,980 --> 00:05:51,530
The companies that build AI

197
00:05:51,570 --> 00:05:52,870
are preparing, too.

198
00:05:53,180 --> 00:05:54,680
This fall, they were reported

199
00:05:54,720 --> 00:05:55,890
to be rehearsing a day

200
00:05:55,930 --> 00:05:56,930
of their own.

201
00:05:57,100 --> 00:05:59,470
The day after an AI disaster.

202
00:05:59,740 --> 00:06:00,740
The day the public

203
00:06:00,780 --> 00:06:02,010
and the politicians

204
00:06:02,050 --> 00:06:03,130
turn against them.

205
00:06:03,510 --> 00:06:05,010
Already, more Americans

206
00:06:05,050 --> 00:06:06,640
oppose an AI data center

207
00:06:06,680 --> 00:06:07,590
near their home

208
00:06:07,630 --> 00:06:09,480
than a nuclear power plant.

209
00:06:10,090 --> 00:06:12,390
To be fair: for some owners,

210
00:06:12,430 --> 00:06:14,540
a bunker is just insurance.

211
00:06:14,720 --> 00:06:16,920
Or a very expensive hobby.

212
00:06:17,180 --> 00:06:18,270
The two owners you heard

213
00:06:18,310 --> 00:06:20,760
from say storms and bombs.

214
00:06:20,850 --> 00:06:21,850
Not people.

215
00:06:22,020 --> 00:06:24,330
And one AI company says its drills

216
00:06:24,370 --> 00:06:26,570
are practice, not a prediction.

217
00:06:26,800 --> 00:06:28,200
But follow the trail.

218
00:06:28,490 --> 00:06:29,250
Guards.

219
00:06:29,290 --> 00:06:30,070
Locks.

220
00:06:30,110 --> 00:06:31,370
Mutiny plans.

221
00:06:31,520 --> 00:06:33,350
None of that stops a storm.

222
00:06:33,530 --> 00:06:34,530
Or a bomb.

223
00:06:34,620 --> 00:06:35,680
Or a machine.

224
00:06:35,920 --> 00:06:37,780
It's built against people.

225
00:06:38,790 --> 00:06:40,820
They're not hiding from the AI.

226
00:06:40,880 --> 00:06:42,470
They're hiding from us.

227
00:06:42,590 --> 00:06:43,530
From a world where

228
00:06:43,570 --> 00:06:45,050
the gains of this technology

229
00:06:45,090 --> 00:06:46,350
go to a few,

230
00:06:46,390 --> 00:06:48,510
and everyone else gets angry.

231
00:06:48,870 --> 00:06:49,750
You probably don't

232
00:06:49,790 --> 00:06:51,150
feel like a threat.

233
00:06:51,410 --> 00:06:52,970
But from behind that door,

234
00:06:53,040 --> 00:06:54,600
the fear makes sense.

235
00:06:54,950 --> 00:06:56,050
So what would make

236
00:06:56,090 --> 00:06:57,790
the bunker unnecessary?

237
00:06:58,960 --> 00:07:00,030
This channel exists

238
00:07:00,070 --> 00:07:01,860
for one reason: so that

239
00:07:01,900 --> 00:07:03,610
the arrival of superintelligence

240
00:07:03,650 --> 00:07:05,400
goes well for everybody.

241
00:07:05,580 --> 00:07:07,180
On both sides of that door.

242
00:07:07,480 --> 00:07:08,480
Want that too?

243
00:07:08,540 --> 00:07:09,590
Then subscribe.

244
00:07:10,800 --> 00:07:12,500
Remember the answer those five

245
00:07:12,540 --> 00:07:13,970
men rolled their eyes at?

246
00:07:14,420 --> 00:07:16,410
Treat your guards like friends.

247
00:07:16,530 --> 00:07:17,530
Right now.

248
00:07:17,770 --> 00:07:19,830
Invest, Rushkoff told them,

249
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:21,990
"in people and relationships."

250
00:07:22,170 --> 00:07:23,050
Scale that up,

251
00:07:23,090 --> 00:07:24,920
and it stops sounding soft.

252
00:07:25,250 --> 00:07:26,210
The best protection

253
00:07:26,250 --> 00:07:27,790
isn't a thicker door.

254
00:07:27,890 --> 00:07:28,930
It's a world nobody

255
00:07:28,970 --> 00:07:30,150
wants to storm.

256
00:07:30,500 --> 00:07:31,580
One country has built

257
00:07:31,620 --> 00:07:33,150
safety for everyone.

258
00:07:33,300 --> 00:07:34,340
In concrete.

259
00:07:34,570 --> 00:07:35,910
Switzerland made it a rule

260
00:07:35,950 --> 00:07:38,230
decades ago: a protected place

261
00:07:38,270 --> 00:07:39,770
for every resident.

262
00:07:40,330 --> 00:07:41,870
Today it has more shelter

263
00:07:41,910 --> 00:07:43,300
places than people.

264
00:07:43,600 --> 00:07:44,930
Some are wine cellars

265
00:07:44,970 --> 00:07:46,900
or party rooms in the meantime.

266
00:07:47,370 --> 00:07:49,720
In Helsinki, Finland, the shelters

267
00:07:49,760 --> 00:07:51,110
double as playgrounds

268
00:07:51,150 --> 00:07:52,390
and swimming pools.

269
00:07:53,400 --> 00:07:54,690
A bunker for a few

270
00:07:54,730 --> 00:07:56,140
is a hiding place.

271
00:07:56,330 --> 00:07:57,730
A bunker for everyone

272
00:07:57,770 --> 00:07:58,910
is a society.

273
00:07:59,200 --> 00:08:00,160
But those shelters are

274
00:08:00,200 --> 00:08:01,750
built against bombs.

275
00:08:01,900 --> 00:08:03,380
A bunker against people

276
00:08:03,420 --> 00:08:05,290
never has room for everyone.

277
00:08:05,450 --> 00:08:07,380
Someone has to stay outside.

278
00:08:07,600 --> 00:08:09,900
So a world nobody wants to storm

279
00:08:09,940 --> 00:08:11,830
can't be poured in concrete.

280
00:08:11,990 --> 00:08:12,950
And how to build it

281
00:08:12,990 --> 00:08:14,270
is an open argument.

282
00:08:14,550 --> 00:08:15,560
Tristan Harris has

283
00:08:15,600 --> 00:08:16,830
the shortest answer:

284
00:08:23,630 --> 00:08:25,700
One has already been written.

285
00:08:26,080 --> 00:08:28,070
If AI shakes up the job market

286
00:08:28,110 --> 00:08:30,370
in America, a bill in the Senate

287
00:08:30,410 --> 00:08:31,980
would pay people who lose their

288
00:08:32,020 --> 00:08:33,790
jobs at least three quarters

289
00:08:33,830 --> 00:08:35,860
of their wage, for half a year.

290
00:08:36,340 --> 00:08:38,090
Others bet on the companies.

291
00:08:38,450 --> 00:08:39,740
Microsoft has promised

292
00:08:39,780 --> 00:08:41,000
its new data centers

293
00:08:41,040 --> 00:08:42,420
will pay their own way,

294
00:08:42,490 --> 00:08:43,880
so the neighbors don't.

295
00:08:44,430 --> 00:08:45,800
Neither is done.

296
00:08:46,040 --> 00:08:47,770
The bill hasn't passed.

297
00:08:47,900 --> 00:08:49,580
The promise isn't a law.

298
00:08:49,870 --> 00:08:51,690
That world isn't built yet.

299
00:08:51,940 --> 00:08:52,990
Whether it will be

300
00:08:53,030 --> 00:08:54,790
is decided by lawmakers,

301
00:08:54,830 --> 00:08:56,910
by companies, and by voters.

302
00:08:58,080 --> 00:08:59,910
So go back to that door.

303
00:09:00,040 --> 00:09:01,930
The one that only opens for a few.

304
00:09:02,240 --> 00:09:03,510
Now you know the reason.

305
00:09:03,690 --> 00:09:04,730
Not the machine.

306
00:09:04,930 --> 00:09:07,300
The fear of everyone left outside.

307
00:09:07,480 --> 00:09:08,480
And that fear points

308
00:09:08,520 --> 00:09:09,700
at something true.

309
00:09:09,940 --> 00:09:11,250
A future where a few win

310
00:09:11,290 --> 00:09:12,930
everything isn't safe.

311
00:09:13,140 --> 00:09:14,410
Not even for the few.

312
00:09:14,750 --> 00:09:15,710
The safe one leaves

313
00:09:15,750 --> 00:09:17,030
no one outside.

314
00:09:18,060 --> 00:09:19,300
You can't build a bunker

315
00:09:19,340 --> 00:09:21,170
for 8 billion people.

316
00:09:21,480 --> 00:09:22,860
You can only build a world

317
00:09:22,900 --> 00:09:24,560
where nobody needs one.

318
00:09:25,660 --> 00:09:26,720
This channel exists

319
00:09:26,760 --> 00:09:28,500
for one reason: so that

320
00:09:28,540 --> 00:09:30,250
the arrival of superintelligence

321
00:09:30,290 --> 00:09:32,050
goes well for everybody.

322
00:09:32,230 --> 00:09:33,960
All 8 billion of us.

323
00:09:34,180 --> 00:09:35,180
Want that too?

324
00:09:35,270 --> 00:09:36,270
Then subscribe.

